  "id": "assisted-reproductive-technology",
  "term": "assisted reproductive technology",
  "definition": "Assisted reproductive technology is a group of medical procedures used to help people conceive when spontaneous conception is difficult or unsuccessful. In the psychology literature, it is discussed not only as a fertility treatment but also as an experience that can involve significant emotional strain, including anxiety during treatment and around pregnancy.",
